<BaseLayout title="About OPTCGTools" description="Learn why OPTCGTools is a small, math-only suite for ONE PIECE Card Game board and deck decisions.">
  <section class="page-intro"><div class="shell"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>›</span><span>About</span></nav><h1>About <span style="color: var(--gold)">OPTCGTools</span></h1><p>An independent, browser-based set of narrow math utilities for ONE PIECE Card Game players.</p></div></section>
  <section class="content-section"><div class="shell"><span class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--red)"><Anchor size={15} /> Why it exists</span><h2>Less guessing around the useful parts.</h2><p>OPTCGTools exists to make the small pieces of game math easier to inspect: whether a declared counter pool holds, how an attack sequence taxes it, and how often a deck sees a set of copies. It does not position a generic calculation as card-specific expertise.</p><p>The suite deliberately has no card database, account system, deck uploads, or personalized recommendations. That keeps inputs quick, makes the assumptions visible, and avoids collecting player data just to answer a math question.</p><h3>How the site earns trust</h3><ul><li>Rules claims are versioned and linked to the official English Comprehensive Rules.</li><li>Every calculator includes its constraints at the result - not just in a hidden disclaimer.</li><li>Core formulas have fixture tests that can be re-run with the project.</li><li>Website content never claims affiliation with Bandai, Shueisha, or the ONE PIECE Card Game.</li></ul><h3>Scope</h3><p>This is a static, global, English-language tool site. It makes no search-volume claims, player-count claims, gameplay advice guarantees, or tournament-ruling promises. For a card interaction, use the current card text and official resources.</p><p><a href="/rules-and-method/">Review the rules snapshot and methodology →</a></p></div></section>
  <section class="content-section tint"><div class="shell split"><div><span class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--red)"><Compass size={15} /> Product principle</span><h2>Useful even if a search engine never saw it.</h2><p>The first priority is a fast answer on a phone: a tool, local calculation, readable result, and an honest explanation of what the result cannot know.</p></div><div class="feature-list"><div class="feature"><span class="feature-icon"><ShieldCheck size={18} /></span><div><h3>Independent fan project</h3><p>Not affiliated with Bandai, Shueisha, or the ONE PIECE Card Game.</p></div></div><div class="feature"><span class="feature-icon"><Anchor size={18} /></span><div><h3>Math, not a database</h3><p>Bring your own state, card text, and judgment - this site handles the arithmetic.</p></div></div></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
